.TH TEATHER-HELPER 8 "August 2026" "Teather 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
teather-helper \- privileged Teather tunnel launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/libexec/teather-helper run
.I LOOPBACK_PORT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teather-helper
is an internal, root-owned helper invoked through polkit. It validates its caller,
arguments, loopback proxy, and route state; opens a nonpersistent TUN interface;
then drops privileges before executing the tunnel process with an inherited file
descriptor. It is not intended to be run directly.
.PP
The helper refuses ambiguous interfaces, routes, VPN policy, and default-route
preference. It does not alter system DNS, NetworkManager, firewall rules, policy
rules, or physical interfaces.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/teather/RECOVERY.md.gz
Offline inspection and recovery instructions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR teather (1)
